			<div class="content" id="post-content-1502080">
									

<p>&quot;Holy pedantic footnotes Batman!&quot;</p>
<p>I can see that you put a lot of work into this one, and technically speaking there are few articles that rival it. However this article suffers from some failings that really bring it down.</p>
<p>The footnotes: Way too many. I feel like I'm reading the idiot's version of Paradise Lost again. Aside from the one (whose existence is dubious at this moment) kid who made it impossible for someone to write about him, I have <em>never</em> seen so many footnotes. In this case, is starts to border on being a bad thing, and it becomes more of a chore to read them; most of the time they barely add to the text. The [REDACTED] you used is okay in small quantities, and I think you used it well, but then you started in with <em>way</em> too much of it towards the end.</p>
<p>Also, the concept. It doesn't really do anything for me. In summary, it's &quot;typewriter what types things what do some odd thing to people when they read it&quot;. It really doesn't pique my curiosity, as the effects are often mild and while there are some exciting ones, they are bogged down and weakened by the sheer volume of text which tends to err on the boring side.</p>
<p>You have good stuff in there somewhere, but it is buried under dull text and technical (also dull) writing. If you clean it up and put more of an edge on it, I would love to upvote it, but right now it feels like a mess.</p>

							</div>

								
					
