<p>More or less agreeing with Hyenaboy; I sort of assume that each SCP has its own experiment file, in which things like the exact poem typed up using SCP-1804, or the original designations of works associated with it, are listed. My understanding was that the point of an SCP file is to provide what information is relevant to <em>containing</em> the object, not to list everything the Foundation knows about the object. But you [sandrewswann] have been around considerably longer than I have, so you're probably in a better position to say whether that's actually the case.</p>
<p>I'm fairly neutral on the concept itself; you've supported it well, and it's an effect that seems logical, given the physical form of the SCP, but there's nothing about it that's particularly surprising after the first paragraph of the description. (&quot;Turns out that was not a great idea&quot; made me chuckle a little.)</p>

